                    },
                    "message": "Why are you continuing in case of an error? Can you please add a comment explaining the reasoning if this is intentional?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/oemcommands.cpp",
                    "line": 701,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Liora Guo",
                        "email": "liora.guo.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "LioraGuo-wiwynn"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @paligill@gmail.com,\nThanks for the reminder! I initially considered keeping a fallback, but I agree that returning immediately on a D-Bus error is safer and prevents misreporting. The debug card refreshes via IPMI about every 5 seconds, which serves as a natural retry without risking an unsafe fallback. Already resolved in PATCH 8."
                }
